BASound provides a glue layer between the Linux ALSA driver code and the
FreeBSD sound(4) subsystem.  It allows ALSA-based drivers for professional
and pro-consumer audio hardware to be used on FreeBSD without modifying
the FreeBSD kernel sources or the upstream ALSA drivers.

Supported device families:

  - DICE FireWire audio interfaces (Weiss, Focusrite, TC Electronic,
    Alesis, M-Audio, PreSonus, and others)
  - RME Hammerfall DSP PCI interfaces (Digiface, Multiface, 9652)
  - Digidesign Digi 002/003 FireWire interfaces
  - Line6 USB audio interfaces (POD, TonePort, Variax)
  - M-Audio MIDISport 8x8 USB MIDI interface

The port installs a core module (basound.ko) and one module per device
class.  Only load the module matching your hardware.
